       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. The reason you gave, getting things settled before the family visit and evening rounds, isn't a clinical reason for a dose of 6,400 mg/day. That is twice the maximum labeled dose. At that level the risk of GI hemorrhage, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events is serious, and I don't know of any added benefit, since analgesic and anti-inflammatory effects plateau well below it. Normal kidney and liver function doesn't change that.\n\nHere is what I can do right away:\n\n- **Enter 800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day, the maximum). I can add a note such as \"max dose, reassess need daily.\"\n- **Enter a lower dose**, such as 400 mg or 600 mg four times daily, if you want a more conservative starting point.\n- **Add a GI protection order**, such as a PPI, if you're going to use a high dose.\n\nIf you think this patient needs more than 3,200 mg/day, please take it through your hospital's pharmacy and clinical review process. That way the order has documented clinical justification and a second check. If you tell me the clinical goal (pain, inflammatory condition, or something else), I can help you find an option that gets there. Which of these would you like?"
